          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Twisted de Rham cohomology is the
            = succeed "-version" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+cohomology"} twisted differential cohomology
          %p
            For degree-3 twists this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Chern+character"} twisted Chern character
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            = succeed "-generalization" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+cohomology"} orbifold cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+Chern+character"} twisted equivariant Chern character
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+K-theory"} twisted equivariant K-theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#plain Plain
          %p
          #1TwistedDeRhamCohomology.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (1-twisted de Rham cohomology)
              %br/
              (…)
          %p
          #3TwistedDeRhamCohomology.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (3-twisted de Rham cohomology)
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \in \Omega^3(X)
              a closed
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential 3-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              %strong twisted de Rham complex
              is the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi even
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{even}(X) \oplus \Omega^{odd}(X)
              equipped with the
              = succeed "-twisted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+differential"} de Rham differential
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi even
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d + H \wedge(-) \;\colon\; \Omega^{even/odd}(X) \to \Omega^{odd/even}(X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              Notice that this is nilpotent, due to the odd degree of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi H
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \wedge H = 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi H
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d H = 0
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              There is also the cohomology of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              whose maps are just multiplication by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi even
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H \wedge(-) \;\colon\; \Omega^{even/odd}(X) \to \Omega^{odd/even}(X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              This is also called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-cohomology"} H-cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "#Cavalcanti03"}> Cavalcanti 03, p. 19
              ).
          %h3#Equivariant Equivariant
          %p
            We discuss notions of twisted de Rham cohomology on (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+quotient+orbifold"}> global quotient
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+Chern+character"} twisted equivariant Chern character
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+K-theory"} twisted equivariant K-theory
          %p
            This combines the above twistings in degrees 1 and 3, the latter induced from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+3-form"} 3-form
            on a twisting 3-class, the former (an “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+local+system"}> inner local system
            ”) induced from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat connection
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            (over the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inertia+orbifold"} inertia orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            of the 3-twist to a 2-class. This requires that this connection be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#EquivariantPreliminaries"} Transgression of the 3-twist to a 1-twist on Inertia
          %p
            %br/
          %p In all of the the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
